>> title: Panang Curry Paste
>> category: Spice Blends & Marinades
>> tags: thai, peanuts, paste, chiles, curry
>> counters: Thai Kitchen
>> aka: prik gaeng panang, phanaeng paste, penang curry paste, panang paste, gaeng panang paste, panang curry paste
>> pairs-with: panang-curry
>> servings: 8
>> time: 45 min
>> slack: narrow — the peanuts are toasted separately and watched, because a dark nut is bitter and here the nut is the sweetness
>> step.1: soak 20 min, drain and chop
>> step.2: toast 2 min, grind in a mortar
>> step.3: pound to a fibrous paste
>> step.4: pound in
>> step.5: work in

Soak @dried long red chiles{8}(stemmed and seeded) in hot water for ~soak{20%min}, then drain and chop them.

Toast @coriander seeds{2%Tbs}, @cumin seeds{1%tsp} and @white peppercorns{1%tsp} in a dry #skillet{} over medium heat for ~toast{2%min}, then grind them to a powder in a #mortar{}.

Pound @&(~2)soaked chiles{} with @kosher salt{1%tsp}, @lemongrass{2%stalks}(tender parts only, thinly sliced), @galangal{2%tsp}(peeled and chopped), @makrut lime zest{1%tsp} and @coriander root{1%Tbs}(scrubbed and chopped) to a fibrous paste.

Pound @garlic{8%cloves} and @shallots{4}(chopped) into @&(~1)paste{}.

Work @&(~3)ground spices{}, @roasted peanuts{1/4%cup}(ground fine) and @shrimp paste{1%Tbs}(kapi) into @&(~1)paste{} until it is smooth and heavy.
